(function(E){ const x = E["hr-m4"] = E["hr-m4"] || {units:{}}; x.units["hr-4-3"] = {"explain":{"id":"c-hr-4-3-e","course":"hr","unit":"hr-4-3","type":"explain","level":"B1","title":{"en":"Hearing a complaint","tr":"Bir şikâyeti dinlemek","fa":"شنیدن یک شکایت"},"objective":{"en":"After this lesson, you can listen to a complaint, summarise it back and agree the next steps.","tr":"Bu dersin sonunda bir şikâyeti dinleyip karşı tarafa özetleyebilecek ve sonraki adımlarda anlaşabileceksin.","fa":"بعد از این درس می‌توانی به یک شکایت گوش بدهی، خلاصه‌اش را به خود فرد بگویی و درباره‌ی قدم‌های بعدی به توافق برسی."},"hook":{"en":"Summarise a complaint before you answer, because the person first needs to know you heard them. Leyla had every answer ready. She stopped and summarised Arash first. Then he sat down.","tr":"Cevap vermeden önce şikâyeti özetle, çünkü kişi önce duyulduğunu bilmek ister. Leyla’nın bütün cevapları hazırdı. Durdu ve önce Arash’ın söylediklerini özetledi. O zaman Arash oturdu.","fa":"قبل از جواب دادن، شکایت را خلاصه کن، چون آن شخص اول باید بداند حرفش را شنیده‌ای. لیلا همه‌ی جواب‌ها را آماده داشت. دست نگه داشت و اول حرف‌های آرش را خلاصه کرد. آن وقت آرش نشست."},"before":{"en":"Write a follow-up to someone who complained: their main point in your own words, their feeling, and the next step.","tr":"Şikâyet eden birine takip mesajı yaz: ana noktasını kendi sözlerinle, hissettiğini ve bir sonraki adımı.","fa":"برای کسی که شکایت کرده یک پیام پیگیری بنویس: حرف اصلی‌اش با کلمه‌های خودت، احساسش و قدم بعدی."},"rounds":[[1,4],[2,3]],"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Key points","tr":"Ana nokta","fa":"نکته‌ی اصلی"},"value":"4"},{"label":{"en":"Key phrases","tr":"Anahtar ifade","fa":"عبارت کلیدی"},"value":"5"},{"label":{"en":"Practice tasks","tr":"Alıştırma","fa":"تمرین"},"value":"4"}],"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"The skill","tr":"Beceri","fa":"مهارت"},"head":{"en":"Summarise before you answer","tr":"Cevap vermeden önce özetle","fa":"قبل از جواب دادن خلاصه کن"},"body":{"en":"People repeat a complaint until they feel heard. So listen to the end and say it back in your own words. Name the feeling. Only then agree the next steps.","tr":"İnsanlar duyulduklarını hissedene kadar şikâyetlerini tekrarlar. Bu yüzden sonuna kadar dinle ve kendi kelimelerinle geri söyle. Duygunun adını koy. Sonraki adımlarda ancak ondan sonra anlaşın.","fa":"آدم‌ها تا حس نکنند حرفشان شنیده شده، شکایت را تکرار می‌کنند. پس تا آخر گوش بده و حرفش را با کلمه‌های خودت تکرار کن. بگو چه احساسی دارد. فقط بعد از آن درباره‌ی قدم‌های بعدی توافق کن."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The language","tr":"Dil","fa":"زبان"},"head":{"en":"Summarising feelings: it sounds (like)..., so what you're saying is...","tr":"Duyguları özetlemek: it sounds (like)..., so what you're saying is...","fa":"خلاصه کردن احساس‌ها: it sounds (like)..."},"steps":[{"en":"For a feeling word: sound + adjective.","tr":"Bir duygu kelimesi için: sound + sıfat.","fa":"برای گفتن احساس، بعد از sound صفت می‌آید.","ex":"That sounds really frustrating."},{"en":"For a full idea: sound like + clause or noun.","tr":"Tam bir fikir için: sound like + yan cümle ya da isim.","fa":"برای یک فکر کامل، بعد از sound like جمله یا اسم می‌آید.","ex":"It sounds like you weren't told about the change."},{"en":"-ing for the situation, -ed for the person.","tr":"Durum için -ing, kişi için -ed.","fa":"برای موقعیت صفت -ing‌دار بیاور و برای آدم صفت -ed‌دار.","ex":"a frustrating month / you feel frustrated"},{"en":"Summarise before you reply.","tr":"Cevap vermeden önce özetle.","fa":"پیش از جواب دادن خلاصه کن.","ex":"So what you're saying is that your team has covered extra shifts."}],"table":{"headers":{"en":["Pattern","Example"],"tr":["Kalıp","Örnek"],"fa":["الگو","مثال"]},"rows":[["sound + adjective","That sounds frustrating."],["sound like + clause","It sounds like nobody asked your team first."],["person + -ed adjective","You must feel frustrated."],["summary","So what you're saying is (that)..."]]},"tip":{"en":"Turkish 'sinir bozucu gibi' and Persian 'be nazar khaste-konande miad' use one pattern for everything, so learners write 'sounds like frustrating'. English splits sound + adjective and sound like + clause.","tr":"Türkçede 'çok sinir bozucu gibi görünüyor' deriz ve 'gibi' her şeyle gelir; bu yüzden 'sounds like frustrating' yazılır. İngilizcede sıfattan önce like gelmez: It sounds frustrating.","fa":"در فارسی می‌گوییم «به نظر خیلی آزاردهنده است» و یک الگو برای همه چیز داریم؛ برای همین بعضی‌ها می‌نویسند «sounds like frustrating». در انگلیسی پیش از صفت like نمی‌آید: «⁨It sounds frustrating.⁩»"},"wrong":"That sounds like frustrating.","right":"That sounds frustrating."},{"eyebrow":{"en":"Key phrases","tr":"Anahtar ifadeler","fa":"عبارت‌های کلیدی"},"head":{"en":"Phrases for this task","tr":"Bu görev için ifadeler","fa":"عبارت‌های این کار"},"phrases":[{"phrase":"Can I check I've understood?","meaning":{"en":"Opens a summary.","tr":"Bir özeti başlatır.","fa":"خلاصه کردن را شروع می‌کند."}},{"phrase":"It sounds like you feel...","meaning":{"en":"Names the feeling.","tr":"Duyguyu adlandırır.","fa":"احساس طرف را نام می‌برد."}},{"phrase":"What would a good outcome look like for you?","meaning":{"en":"Moves towards next steps.","tr":"Sonraki adımlara geçer.","fa":"گفتگو را به سمت قدم‌های بعدی می‌برد."}},{"phrase":"complaint","meaning":{"en":"A statement that something is wrong or unfair.","tr":"şikâyet.","fa":"شکایت؛ گلایه"}},{"phrase":"summarise","meaning":{"en":"To give the main points briefly.","tr":"özetlemek.","fa":"خلاصه کردن"}}]},{"eyebrow":{"en":"At work","tr":"İş yerinde","fa":"در محیط کار"},"head":{"en":"Respect the years of service","tr":"Kıdeme saygı göster","fa":"به سابقه‌ی کارش احترام بگذار"},"body":{"en":"In the UK a formal written complaint at work is usually called a \"grievance\" and follows a set procedure, but an early informal conversation often solves the problem. In many workplaces in Turkey, Iran and the Persian Gulf, long-serving staff expect respect for their years of service; naming those years out loud can matter as much as the solution.","tr":"Birleşik Krallık'ta işyerindeki resmî yazılı şikâyete genellikle \"grievance\" denir ve belirli bir prosedürü vardır; ama erken ve gayriresmî bir konuşma çoğu zaman sorunu çözer. Türkiye, İran ve Basra Körfezi'ndeki birçok işyerinde kıdemli çalışanlar hizmet yıllarına saygı bekler; bu yılları açıkça dile getirmek çözüm kadar önemli olabilir.","fa":"در بریتانیا به شکایت رسمی و کتبی در محل کار معمولاً grievance می‌گویند و روال مشخصی دارد، اما یک گفتگوی غیررسمی در همان ابتدا اغلب مشکل را حل می‌کند. در بسیاری از محیط‌های کاری ترکیه، ایران و کشورهای حاشیه‌ی خلیج فارس، کارکنان قدیمی انتظار دارند به سابقه‌شان احترام گذاشته شود؛ اینکه سال‌های خدمتشان را به زبان بیاوری ممکن است به اندازه‌ی خودِ راه‌حل مهم باشد."}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"From weak to strong","tr":"Zayıftan güçlüye","fa":"از راه‌حل زودهنگام تا خلاصه کردن"},"text":"Facts: The person has worked every Saturday since May. Nobody asked them first.","item":"Don't worry, that's normal. Everyone does overtime.","why":{"en":"Weak: a solution too early. Strong: facts and feeling first.","tr":"Zayıf: çok erken bir çözüm. Güçlü: önce olgular ve duygu.","fa":"در نسخه‌ی اول راه‌حل خیلی زود می‌آید. نسخه‌ی دوم اول واقعیت‌ها و احساس را می‌گوید."},"answer":"So you've worked every Saturday since May, and nobody asked. That sounds exhausting.","cut":["Don't worry, that's normal.","Everyone does overtime."],"cutHint":{"en":"Tap what tells the person their problem does not count.","tr":"Kişiye sorununun önemsiz olduğunu söyleyen sözlere dokun.","fa":"روی حرف‌هایی بزن که به آن آدم می‌گویند مشکلش مهم نیست."}},"quick":{"prompt":"A driver with twenty years at the company complains about the new rota. What can matter as much as the solution?","options":["Naming his years of service with respect","Telling him the rule is the same for everyone","Asking him to put it in writing first"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"Naming his years of service: in many workplaces in Turkey, Iran and the Persian Gulf, long-serving staff expect that respect.","tr":"Hizmet yıllarını saygıyla anmak: Türkiye’de, İran’da ve Basra Körfezi’nde birçok iş yerinde uzun süredir çalışanlar bu saygıyı bekler.","fa":"اینکه سال‌های خدمتش را با احترام به زبان بیاوری: در خیلی از محیط‌های کاری ترکیه، ایران و خلیج فارس، کارمندانِ باسابقه این احترام را انتظار دارند."},"point":4,"hint2":{"en":"Think about what twenty years at one company means to someone. What do they want to hear first?","tr":"Bir şirkette yirmi yılın birisi için ne anlama geldiğini düşün. Önce ne duymak ister?","fa":"فکر کن بیست سال کار در یک شرکت برای آدم چه معنایی دارد. اول دوست دارد چه چیزی بشنود؟"}},"remember":{"en":"After sounds, is the next word an adjective? No like. A person or a clause? Add like. Result of this lesson: you can summarise a complaint and agree next steps. You also have a follow-up email.","tr":"sounds'tan sonraki kelime sıfat mı? like yok. Bir kişi ya da yan cümle mi? like ekle. Bu dersin sonucu: bir şikâyeti özetleyip sonraki adımlarda anlaşabilirsin ve elinde bir takip e-postası olur.","fa":"کلمه‌ی بعد از sounds صفت است؟ like نمی‌خواهد. شخص یا جمله است؟ like اضافه کن. حالا می‌توانی شکایتی را خلاصه کنی و درباره‌ی قدم‌های بعدی توافق کنی. ایمیل پیگیری هم آماده است."},"b2Point":{"eyebrow":{"en":"B2 track","tr":"B2 yolu","fa":"مسیر B2"},"head":{"en":"Tentative reflecting: sounds as though, seem to have been","tr":"Temkinli yansıtma: sounds as though, seem to have been","fa":"بازتاب محتاطانه: sounds as though، seem to have been"},"steps":[{"en":"Softer reflecting: sounds as though / as if + clause.","tr":"Daha yumuşak yansıtma: sounds as though / as if + yan cümle.","fa":"برای بازتاب نرم‌تر، بعد از sounds as though یا as if یک جمله بیاور.","ex":"It sounds as though nobody asked your team first."},{"en":"Something before now: seem to have + past participle.","tr":"Şimdiden önce olan: seem to have + past participle.","fa":"برای چیزی که قبلاً رخ داده، seem to have و اسم مفعول را به کار ببر.","ex":"You seem to have been left out of the decision."},{"en":"The person still feels -ed.","tr":"Kişi yine -ed hisseder.","fa":"برای احساس آدم، باز هم صفت -ed‌دار می‌آید.","ex":"It sounds as though you feel frustrated."}],"table":{"headers":{"en":["Pattern","Example"],"tr":["Kalıp","Örnek"],"fa":["الگو","مثال"]},"rows":[["It sounds as though + clause","It sounds as though nobody asked your team first."],["seem to have + past participle","You seem to have been left out of the decision."],["appear to have + past participle","The request appears to have been lost."]]},"body":{"en":"B2 track: in your summary to Arash, use one \"sounds as though\" and one \"seem to have been\" sentence.","tr":"B2 yolu: Arash'a yaptığın özette bir \"sounds as though\" ve bir \"seem to have been\" cümlesi kullan.","fa":"مسیر B2: در خلاصه‌ای که برای آرش می‌گویی، یک جمله با «sounds as though» و یک جمله با «seem to have been» بیاور."}},"source":{"en":"Informed by the Acas Code of Practice on grievances.","tr":"Acas’ın şikâyet süreçleriyle ilgili uygulama kurallarından yararlanır.","fa":"با استفاده از آیین‌نامه‌ی Acas درباره‌ی رسیدگی به شکایت."}},"grammar":{"id":"c-hr-4-3-g","level":"B1","course":"hr","unit":"hr-4-3","title":"Summarising feelings: it sounds (like)..., so what you're saying is...","titleTr":"Duyguları özetlemek: it sounds (like)..., so what you're saying is...","exp":{"en":"Before you answer a complaint, show that you heard it. Two patterns do most of the work. First, \"sound\": sound + adjective (\"That sounds frustrating.\") but sound like + a clause or noun (\"It sounds like you weren't told about the change.\"). Not \"sounds like frustrating\". Use the -ing adjective for the situation (frustrating, worrying, tiring) and the -ed adjective for the person (\"You must feel frustrated.\"). Second, a summary: \"So what you're saying is (that) your team has covered extra shifts since March.\" Keep the normal statement order after \"is\". Summarise feelings and reasons before you give any reply or solution.","tr":"Bir şikâyete cevap vermeden önce onu duyduğunu göster. İki kalıp işin çoğunu görür. Birincisi \"sound\": sound + sıfat (\"That sounds frustrating.\"), ama sound like + yan cümle veya isim (\"It sounds like you weren't told about the change.\"). \"sounds like frustrating\" değil. Durum için -ing sıfatını (frustrating, worrying, tiring), kişi için -ed sıfatını kullan (\"You must feel frustrated.\"). İkincisi özet: \"So what you're saying is (that) your team has covered extra shifts since March.\" \"is\"ten sonra düz cümle sırasını koru. Herhangi bir cevap ya da çözüm vermeden önce duyguları ve sebepleri özetle.","fa":"قبل از اینکه به یک شکایت جواب بدهی، نشان بده که حرف طرف را شنیده‌ای. بیشتر این کار را دو الگو انجام می‌دهند. اول، فعل ⁨sound⁩: بعد از ⁨sound⁩ صفت می‌آید («⁨That sounds frustrating.⁩»)، اما بعد از ⁨sound like⁩ جمله یا اسم («⁨It sounds like you weren't told about the change.⁩»). پس «⁨sounds like frustrating⁩» غلط است. برای توصیف موقعیت از صفت ⁨-ing⁩ استفاده کن (⁨frustrating⁩، ⁨worrying⁩، ⁨tiring⁩) و برای توصیف حال آدم از صفت ⁨-ed⁩: «⁨You must feel frustrated.⁩» دوم، خلاصه کردن: «⁨So what you're saying is (that) your team has covered extra shifts since March.⁩» بعد از ⁨is⁩ ترتیب جمله‌ی خبری را حفظ کن. قبل از هر جواب یا راه‌حلی، اول احساس‌ها و دلیل‌های طرف را خلاصه کن."},"formsTable":{"headers":{"en":["Pattern","Example"],"tr":["Kalıp","Örnek"],"fa":["الگو","مثال"]},"rows":[["sound + adjective","That sounds frustrating."],["sound like + clause","It sounds like nobody asked your team first."],["person + -ed adjective","You must feel frustrated."],["summary","So what you're saying is (that)..."]]},"wrong":"It sounds like frustrating.","right":"It sounds frustrating.","blank":{"sentence":"It sounds ___ you weren't told about the change.","word":"like","distractors":["that","so"]},"wrong2":"So what you saying is the team is tired.","right2":"So what you're saying is that the team is tired.","blank2":{"sentence":"That sounds really ___.","word":"frustrating","distractors":["frustrated","like frustrating"]},"expParts":{"tryFrom":"blank","hook":{"en":"Leyla had every answer ready. She closed her mouth and summarised Arash first. Then he sat down.","tr":"Leyla'nın her cevabı hazırdı. Ağzını kapattı ve önce Arash'ı özetledi. Ancak o zaman Arash oturdu.","fa":"لیلا همه‌ی جواب‌ها را آماده داشت. ولی ساکت ماند و اول حرف آرش را خلاصه کرد. آن وقت آرش نشست."},"tryWhy":{"en":"like: sound like + a clause (you weren't told). Without like, sound needs an adjective.","tr":"like: sound like + yan cümle (you weren't told). like olmadan sound bir sıfat ister.","fa":"جواب like است: بعد از sound like جمله می‌آید (you weren't told). بدون like، بعد از sound صفت لازم است."},"rule":[{"en":"sound + adjective.","tr":"sound + sıfat.","fa":"بعد از sound صفت می‌آید.","ex":"That sounds really frustrating."},{"en":"sound like + clause or noun.","tr":"sound like + yan cümle ya da isim.","fa":"بعد از sound like جمله یا اسم می‌آید.","ex":"It sounds like you weren't told about the change."},{"en":"-ing for the situation, -ed for the person.","tr":"Durum için -ing, kişi için -ed.","fa":"برای موقعیت صفت -ing‌دار بیاور و برای آدم صفت -ed‌دار.","ex":"a frustrating month / you feel frustrated"},{"en":"Summarise before you reply.","tr":"Cevap vermeden önce özetle.","fa":"پیش از جواب دادن خلاصه کن.","ex":"So what you're saying is that your team has covered extra shifts."}],"test":{"en":"After sounds, is the next word an adjective? No like. A person or a clause? Add like.","tr":"sounds'tan sonraki kelime sıfat mı? like yok. Bir kişi ya da yan cümle mi? like ekle.","fa":"کلمه‌ی بعد از sounds صفت است؟ like نمی‌خواهد. شخص یا جمله است؟ like اضافه کن."},"contrast":{"en":"Turkish 'sinir bozucu gibi' and Persian 'be nazar khaste-konande miad' use one pattern for everything, so learners write 'sounds like frustrating'. English splits sound + adjective and sound like + clause.","tr":"Türkçede 'çok sinir bozucu gibi görünüyor' deriz ve 'gibi' her şeyle gelir; bu yüzden 'sounds like frustrating' yazılır. İngilizcede sıfattan önce like gelmez: It sounds frustrating.","fa":"در فارسی می‌گوییم «به نظر خیلی آزاردهنده است» و یک الگو برای همه چیز داریم؛ برای همین بعضی‌ها می‌نویسند «sounds like frustrating». در انگلیسی پیش از صفت like نمی‌آید: «⁨It sounds frustrating.⁩»"}},"errorWatch":[{"find":["sounds like frustrating","sounds like worrying","sounds like difficult","sounds like hard","sounds like tiring","sounds like unfair","it sounds that"],"fix":{"en":"sound + adjective, sound like + clause: 'That sounds frustrating.' / 'It sounds like you weren't told.'","tr":"sound + sıfat, sound like + yan cümle: 'That sounds frustrating.' / 'It sounds like you weren't told.'","fa":"بعد از sound صفت می‌آید و بعد از sound like جمله: «That sounds frustrating.» و «It sounds like you weren't told.»"}},{"find":["what you saying","you feel frustrating","must feel frustrating","you feel tiring"],"fix":{"en":"Say 'what you're saying is', and use -ed for the person: 'you feel frustrated'.","tr":"'what you're saying is' de ve kişi için -ed kullan: 'you feel frustrated'.","fa":"بنویس «⁨what you're saying is⁩» و برای آدم ⁨-ed⁩ بیاور: «⁨you feel frustrated⁩»."}}]},"b2":{"id":"c-hr-4-3-b2","level":"B2","track":"B2","course":"hr","unit":"hr-4-3","title":"Tentative reflecting: sounds as though, seem to have been","titleTr":"Temkinli yansıtma: sounds as though, seem to have been","exp":{"en":"At B2 you can reflect feelings more tentatively, so you never sound as if you are telling someone what they feel. \"It sounds as though nobody asked your team first.\" (as though / as if + clause, a little softer than sounds like). \"You seem to have been left out of the decision.\" uses seem + perfect infinitive (to have + past participle) for something that happened before now. \"You seem to have been told very late.\" Check the form: to have been, not \"to have be\" or \"to been\". And the feeling word stays -ed for the person: \"It sounds as though you feel frustrated\", not \"frustrating\".","tr":"B2 düzeyinde duyguları daha temkinli yansıtabilirsin; böylece hiçbir zaman birine ne hissettiğini söylüyormuş gibi durmazsın. \"It sounds as though nobody asked your team first.\" (as though / as if + yan cümle, sounds like'tan biraz daha yumuşak). \"You seem to have been left out of the decision.\" cümlesi, şimdiden önce olmuş bir şey için seem + perfect infinitive (to have + past participle) kullanır. \"You seem to have been told very late.\" Biçimi kontrol et: to have been; \"to have be\" ya da \"to been\" değil. Kişi için duygu sözcüğü -ed olarak kalır: \"It sounds as though you feel frustrated\", \"frustrating\" değil.","fa":"در سطح ⁨B2⁩ می‌توانی احساس طرف را محتاطانه‌تر بازتاب دهی تا هیچ‌وقت این‌طور به نظر نرسد که به او می‌گویی چه حسی دارد. «⁨It sounds as though nobody asked your team first.⁩» (بعد از ⁨as though⁩ یا ⁨as if⁩ یک جمله‌ی کامل می‌آید و لحنش کمی نرم‌تر از ⁨sounds like⁩ است.) در «⁨You seem to have been left out of the decision.⁩» از ⁨seem⁩ + مصدر کامل (⁨to have⁩ + اسم مفعول) استفاده شده، برای چیزی که قبلاً اتفاق افتاده است؛ یعنی «انگار شما را در این تصمیم نادیده گرفته‌اند». یا: «⁨You seem to have been told very late.⁩» شکل را دقیق بنویس: ⁨to have been⁩، نه «⁨to have be⁩» و نه «⁨to been⁩». کلمه‌ی احساس هم برای آدم همان ⁨-ed⁩ می‌ماند: «⁨It sounds as though you feel frustrated⁩»، نه «⁨frustrating⁩»."},"formsTable":{"headers":{"en":["Pattern","Example"],"tr":["Kalıp","Örnek"],"fa":["الگو","مثال"]},"rows":[["It sounds as though + clause","It sounds as though nobody asked your team first."],["seem to have + past participle","You seem to have been left out of the decision."],["appear to have + past participle","The request appears to have been lost."]]},"wrong":"You seem to have be left out of the decision.","right":"You seem to have been left out of the decision.","blank":{"sentence":"You seem ___ been left out of the decision.","word":"to have","distractors":["having","to"]},"wrong2":"It sounds as though you feel frustrating.","right2":"It sounds as though you feel frustrated.","blank2":{"sentence":"It sounds as ___ nobody asked your team first.","word":"though","distractors":["that","so"]},"useIn":{"en":"B2 track: in your summary to Arash, use one \"sounds as though\" and one \"seem to have been\" sentence.","tr":"B2 yolu: Arash'a yaptığın özette bir \"sounds as though\" ve bir \"seem to have been\" cümlesi kullan.","fa":"مسیر B2: در خلاصه‌ای که برای آرش می‌گویی، یک جمله با «sounds as though» و یک جمله با «seem to have been» بیاور."},"exitItem":{"from":"hr-4-3","kind":"blank","prompt":"It sounds as ___ nobody explained the change to you.","options":["like","though","that"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"though: 'sounds as though' + a clause is a careful guess. 'As like' and 'as that' are not English.","tr":"though: 'sounds as though' + yan cümle dikkatli bir tahmindir. 'As like' ve 'as that' İngilizce değildir.","fa":"though درست است، چون sounds as though و بعد جمله یک حدس محتاطانه است. as like و as that انگلیسی نیستند."},"hint2":{"en":"Sounds as ... is a fixed pair, like as if. Which word can take the place of if here?","tr":"Sounds as ... kalıp bir ikilidir, as if gibi. Burada if’in yerine hangi kelime gelebilir?","fa":"⁨sounds as ...⁩ یک جفتِ ثابت است، مثل ⁨as if⁩. این‌جا کدام کلمه می‌تواند جای ⁨if⁩ بنشیند؟"}},"expParts":{"hook":{"en":"'It sounds as though nobody asked your team first.' Softer still, so you never tell Arash what he feels.","tr":"'It sounds as though nobody asked your team first.' Daha da yumuşak; böylece Arash'a ne hissettiğini asla dayatmazsın.","fa":"«⁨It sounds as though nobody asked your team first.⁩» نرم‌تر از قبل؛ این‌طوری به آرش نمی‌گویی چه احساسی دارد."},"tryWhy":{"en":"though: the phrase is 'as though' or 'as if', followed by a full clause.","tr":"though: kalıp 'as though' ya da 'as if'tir ve ardından tam bir cümle gelir.","fa":"جواب though است: عبارت درست as though یا as if است و بعدش یک جمله‌ی کامل می‌آید."},"rule":[{"en":"Softer reflecting: sounds as though / as if + clause.","tr":"Daha yumuşak yansıtma: sounds as though / as if + yan cümle.","fa":"برای بازتاب نرم‌تر، بعد از sounds as though یا as if یک جمله بیاور.","ex":"It sounds as though nobody asked your team first."},{"en":"Something before now: seem to have + past participle.","tr":"Şimdiden önce olan: seem to have + past participle.","fa":"برای چیزی که قبلاً رخ داده، seem to have و اسم مفعول را به کار ببر.","ex":"You seem to have been left out of the decision."},{"en":"The person still feels -ed.","tr":"Kişi yine -ed hisseder.","fa":"برای احساس آدم، باز هم صفت -ed‌دار می‌آید.","ex":"It sounds as though you feel frustrated."}],"test":{"en":"Check the chain: to + have + been. Any link missing (to been, to have be)? Fix it.","tr":"Zinciri kontrol et: to + have + been. Bir halka eksik mi (to been, to have be)? Düzelt.","fa":"زنجیره را چک کن: to، have و been. حلقه‌ای جا افتاده (to been، to have be)؟ درستش کن."},"contrast":{"en":"Turkish 'karardan dışlanmış gibisin' and Persian 'enghar kenar gozashte shodi' keep this in one verb form. English needs the full chain: seem to have been left out.","tr":"Türkçede 'karardan dışlanmış gibisin' tek bir fiil ekiyle söylenir. İngilizcede tam zincir gerekir: You seem to have been left out.","fa":"در فارسی می‌گوییم «انگار تو را در این تصمیم کنار گذاشته‌اند». انگلیسی زنجیره‌ی کامل را می‌خواهد: «⁨You seem to have been left out.⁩»"}},"errorWatch":[{"find":["to have be","seem to been","seems to been","as though you feel frustrating","as if you feel frustrating"],"fix":{"en":"Use seem to have been + past participle, and -ed for the person: 'You seem to have been left out.'","tr":"seem to have been + past participle kullan, kişi için -ed: 'You seem to have been left out.'","fa":"از seem to have been و اسم مفعول استفاده کن و برای آدم -ed بیاور: «You seem to have been left out.»"}}]},"vocab":{"id":"c-hr-4-3-v","level":"B1","category":"vocab","course":"hr","unit":"hr-4-3","goals":["career"],"title":{"en":"Hearing Complaints","tr":"Şikâyet Dinlemek","fa":"شنیدن شکایت"},"cards":[{"word":"complaint","sentence":"Arash came to HR with a complaint.","meaning":{"en":"A statement that something is wrong or unfair.","tr":"şikâyet.","fa":"شکایت؛ گلایه"}},{"word":"raise a concern","sentence":"Thank you for raising this concern with me.","gap":"raising this concern","accept":["raising this concern","raising a concern","raise a concern"],"meaning":{"en":"To tell someone about a problem.","tr":"bir endişeyi dile getirmek.","fa":"نگرانی یا مشکلی را مطرح کردن"}},{"word":"grievance","sentence":"If talking does not help, he can file a formal grievance.","meaning":{"en":"A formal written complaint at work.","tr":"resmî şikâyet.","fa":"شکایت رسمی و کتبی در محل کار"}},{"word":"acknowledge","sentence":"First acknowledge his feelings, then discuss solutions.","meaning":{"en":"To show you accept that something is true or real.","tr":"kabul etmek; haklılığını teslim etmek.","fa":"به رسمیت شناختن؛ تصدیق کردن"}},{"word":"summarise","sentence":"Let me summarise what I heard.","meaning":{"en":"To give the main points briefly.","tr":"özetlemek.","fa":"خلاصه کردن"}},{"word":"frustrated","sentence":"He felt frustrated after two years of waiting.","meaning":{"en":"Upset because you cannot change something.","tr":"bıkkın, sinirli (değiştiremediğin bir şey yüzünden).","fa":"کلافه؛ دلخور (چون نمی‌توانی چیزی را تغییر دهی)"}},{"word":"overlooked","sentence":"The Istanbul team felt overlooked.","meaning":{"en":"Not noticed or not given attention.","tr":"göz ardı edilmiş.","fa":"نادیده‌گرفته‌شده؛ از قلم‌افتاده"}},{"word":"take something seriously","sentence":"I take this seriously.","gap":"take this seriously","accept":["take this seriously","take something seriously"],"meaning":{"en":"To treat something as important.","tr":"bir şeyi ciddiye almak.","fa":"چیزی را جدی گرفتن"}},{"word":"follow up","sentence":"I'll follow up with you on Friday.","meaning":{"en":"To contact someone again to continue something.","tr":"takip etmek.","fa":"پیگیری کردن"}},{"word":"workload","sentence":"His team's workload has doubled since March.","meaning":{"en":"The amount of work someone has.","tr":"iş yükü.","fa":"حجم کار؛ بار کاری"}}]},"story":{"id":"c-hr-4-3-s","level":"B1","genre":"Workplace","course":"hr","unit":"hr-4-3","title":{"en":"Twenty-Two Years","tr":"Yirmi İki Yıl","fa":"بیست‌ودو سال"},"text":"Arash knocked on Leyla's door at 4:55, five minutes before the end of the day. He had worked in the Istanbul warehouse for twenty-two years. Leyla had worked at Atlas for three.\n\n\"Do you have a minute?\" he asked. It was clear he needed more than a minute.\n\n\"Of course. Please sit down.\"\n\nHe did not sit. \"Since March, two of my drivers have been in Dubai, training your new people. Nobody asked me. My team covers their shifts. We work Saturdays now. Every Saturday.\" He took a breath. \"And the new drivers in Dubai get new trucks, a welcome lunch, a buddy. I have asked for a second forklift for two years. Two years. I have the emails.\"\n\nLeyla wanted to explain. The Dubai trucks came from a different budget. The forklift was not her decision. Every sentence was ready in her mouth. She closed it.\n\n\"Can I check I've understood?\" she said. \"So what you're saying is that your team has covered extra shifts since March, and nobody asked you first.\"\n\n\"Yes.\"\n\n\"And you've asked for a forklift for two years, and it sounds like nobody answered.\"\n\n\"Nobody.\"\n\n\"That sounds really frustrating. It sounds like you feel your team has been overlooked while all the attention goes to Dubai.\"\n\nArash looked at her for a long moment. Then he sat down.\n\n\"Twenty-two years,\" he said, more quietly. \"I don't need a party. I need someone to ask me before they take my drivers.\"\n\nThey talked until six. At the end they agreed two things: Leyla would get the overtime figures by Friday, and they would see the operations director together on Tuesday. It was not a solution yet. But Arash shook her hand at the door, and that was new.","vocab":[{"word":"knock","en":"To hit a door to ask to come in.","tr":"kapıyı çalmak","fa":"در زدن"},{"word":"cover a shift","en":"To work in place of someone else.","tr":"birinin vardiyasını devralmak","fa":"جای کسی شیفت ایستادن"},{"word":"forklift","en":"A small vehicle that lifts heavy boxes.","tr":"forklift","fa":"لیفتراک"},{"word":"budget","en":"Money planned for one purpose.","tr":"bütçe","fa":"بودجه"},{"word":"figures","en":"Numbers, data.","tr":"rakamlar","fa":"ارقام؛ آمار و اعداد"}],"quiz":[{"prompt":"What were Arash's two main reasons for complaining?","options":["Extra shifts without being asked, and no answer about the forklift","Low salary and a long commute","The new trucks were too small"],"correct":0},{"prompt":"Choose the correct sentence.","options":["That sounds really frustrated.","That sounds really frustrating.","That sounds like really frustrating."],"correct":1},{"prompt":"Why did Leyla not explain the budgets first?","options":["She did not know the answer","She wanted to show she had heard him before replying","She was in a hurry"],"correct":1},{"prompt":"When did Arash sit down, and why?","options":["At once, because he was tired","After she summarised his feelings, because he felt heard","After she promised a new forklift"],"correct":1}],"notice":{"en":"Arash comes in angry at 4:55. Leyla has three explanations ready. Watch what she says instead.","tr":"Arash saat 16.55'te öfkeyle içeri giriyor. Leyla'nın üç açıklaması hazır. Onun yerine ne söylediğine dikkat et.","fa":"آرش ساعت ۴:۵۵ با عصبانیت وارد می‌شود. لیلا سه توضیح آماده دارد. دقت کن به‌جایش چه می‌گوید."},"bridge":{"en":"'So what you're saying is...' and 'That sounds really frustrating.' Next: see how these two patterns work.","tr":"'So what you're saying is...' ve 'That sounds really frustrating.' Sırada: bu iki kalıbın nasıl çalıştığını gör.","fa":"«⁨So what you're saying is...⁩» و «⁨That sounds really frustrating.⁩» قدم بعد: ببین این دو الگو چطور کار می‌کنند."}},"speaking":{"id":"hr-4-3","course":"hr","unit":"hr-4-3","topic":{"en":"Summarising a Complaint Before Replying","tr":"Cevap Vermeden Önce Bir Şikâyeti Özetlemek","fa":"خلاصه کردن شکایت پیش از جواب دادن"},"warmup":{"en":"Think of a time you complained and the other person replied too fast. How did it feel?","tr":"Şikâyet ettiğin ve karşındakinin çok hızlı cevap verdiği bir zamanı düşün. Nasıl hissettirdi?","fa":"یک بار را به یاد بیاور که شکایتی کردی و طرف مقابل خیلی زود جواب داد. چه حسی داشتی؟"},"questions":[{"en":"Listen to Arash. Then summarise his feelings in one sentence: \"It sounds like you feel...\"","tr":"Arash'ı dinle. Sonra duygularını tek cümleyle özetle: \"It sounds like you feel...\"","fa":"به حرف‌های آرش گوش کن. بعد احساسش را در یک جمله خلاصه کن: «⁨It sounds like you feel...⁩»"},{"en":"Summarise his two reasons: \"So what you're saying is...\"","tr":"İki sebebini özetle: \"So what you're saying is...\"","fa":"دو دلیلش را خلاصه کن: «⁨So what you're saying is...⁩»"},{"en":"Only now reply: agree one next step and a date.","tr":"Ancak şimdi cevap ver: bir sonraki adım ve bir tarih üzerinde anlaş.","fa":"فقط حالا جواب بده: روی یک قدم بعدی و یک تاریخ با او توافق کن."}],"followups":[{"en":"Say the whole response in 90 seconds, then 60, then 45.","tr":"Cevabının tamamını 90, sonra 60, sonra 45 saniyede söyle.","fa":"کل پاسخت را یک بار در ۹۰ ثانیه، بعد در ۶۰ و بعد در ۴۵ ثانیه بگو."},{"en":"Arash interrupts: \"You're not listening!\" Stay calm and summarise again.","tr":"Arash sözünü kesiyor: \"Beni dinlemiyorsun!\" Sakin kal ve yeniden özetle.","fa":"آرش حرفت را قطع می‌کند: «⁨You're not listening!⁩» آرامشت را حفظ کن و دوباره خلاصه کن."},{"en":"Now summarise a real worry someone told you, with It sounds like.","tr":"Şimdi birinin sana anlattığı gerçek bir kaygıyı It sounds like ile özetle.","fa":"حالا نگرانی واقعی‌ای را که کسی به تو گفته با It sounds like خلاصه کن."}],"expressions":[{"phrase":"Can I check I've understood?","meaning":{"en":"Opens a summary.","tr":"Bir özeti başlatır.","fa":"خلاصه کردن را شروع می‌کند."}},{"phrase":"It sounds like you feel...","meaning":{"en":"Names the feeling.","tr":"Duyguyu adlandırır.","fa":"احساس طرف را نام می‌برد."}},{"phrase":"What would a good outcome look like for you?","meaning":{"en":"Moves towards next steps.","tr":"Sonraki adımlara geçer.","fa":"گفتگو را به سمت قدم‌های بعدی می‌برد."}}],"culture":{"en":"In the UK a formal written complaint at work is usually called a \"grievance\" and follows a set procedure, but an early informal conversation often solves the problem. In many workplaces in Turkey, Iran and the Persian Gulf, long-serving staff expect respect for their years of service; naming those years out loud can matter as much as the solution.","tr":"Birleşik Krallık'ta işyerindeki resmî yazılı şikâyete genellikle \"grievance\" denir ve belirli bir prosedürü vardır; ama erken ve gayriresmî bir konuşma çoğu zaman sorunu çözer. Türkiye, İran ve Basra Körfezi'ndeki birçok işyerinde kıdemli çalışanlar hizmet yıllarına saygı bekler; bu yılları açıkça dile getirmek çözüm kadar önemli olabilir.","fa":"در بریتانیا به شکایت رسمی و کتبی در محل کار معمولاً grievance می‌گویند و روال مشخصی دارد، اما یک گفتگوی غیررسمی در همان ابتدا اغلب مشکل را حل می‌کند. در بسیاری از محیط‌های کاری ترکیه، ایران و کشورهای حاشیه‌ی خلیج فارس، کارکنان قدیمی انتظار دارند به سابقه‌شان احترام گذاشته شود؛ اینکه سال‌های خدمتشان را به زبان بیاوری ممکن است به اندازه‌ی خودِ راه‌حل مهم باشد."},"model":"Can I check I've understood? So what you're saying is that your team has covered extra shifts since March, and nobody asked you first. And you've asked for a second forklift for two years. That sounds really frustrating. It sounds like you feel your team has been overlooked. Here is what I can do: I'll get the overtime figures by Friday, and we'll see the director together on Tuesday.","selfCheck":[{"en":"I summarised his feelings before I replied.","tr":"Cevap vermeden önce duygularını özetledim.","fa":"پیش از جواب دادن احساسش را خلاصه کردم."},{"en":"I summarised his two reasons with 'So what you're saying is...'","tr":"İki nedenini 'So what you're saying is...' ile özetledim.","fa":"دو دلیلش را با «⁨So what you're saying is...⁩» خلاصه کردم."},{"en":"I used sounds + adjective and sounds like + clause correctly.","tr":"sounds + sıfat ve sounds like + yan cümleyi doğru kullandım.","fa":"sounds را با صفت و sounds like را با جمله درست به کار بردم."},{"en":"I ended with one next step and a date.","tr":"Bir sonraki adım ve bir tarihle bitirdim.","fa":"با یک قدم بعدی و یک تاریخ تمام کردم."}]},"writing":{"id":"c-hr-4-3-w","title":{"en":"A follow-up email to Arash","tr":"Arash'a takip e-postası","fa":"ایمیل پیگیری برای آرش"},"course":"hr","unit":"hr-4-3","type":"writing","difficulty":"medium","prompt":{"en":"Write a follow-up email to Arash (70-100 words): thank him, summarise his two points and his feelings, and list the two agreed next steps with dates.","tr":"Arash'a takip e-postası yaz (70-100 kelime): teşekkür et, iki noktasını ve duygularını özetle, kararlaştırılan iki adımı tarihleriyle yaz.","fa":"یک ایمیل پیگیری برای آرش بنویس (۷۰ تا ۱۰۰ کلمه): از او تشکر کن، دو نکته‌اش و احساسش را خلاصه کن و دو قدم بعدی را که روی آن توافق کردی همراه با تاریخ بنویس."},"model":"Dear Arash, Thank you for talking to me so openly today. I want to check that I understood you. You said that your team has covered extra shifts since March for drivers who went to Dubai, and that nobody asked you first. You also said that you have asked for a second forklift for two years. It sounds like your team feels overlooked, and I understand why. As we agreed, I will send you the overtime figures by Friday, and we will meet the operations director together on Tuesday. Best regards, Leyla","frame":"Dear ___, Thank you for ___. I want to check that I understood you. You said that ___, and that ___. You also said that ___. It sounds like ___. As we agreed, I will ___ by ___, and we will ___ on ___. Best regards, ___","words":[{"word":"you said"},{"word":"it sounds like"},{"word":"agreed"}],"minWords":70,"minSentences":6,"rubric":["Task done: thanks, two points, feeling, two next steps with dates","Organised: summary before action","Language: reported speech; sounds like + clause; will for promises","Tone: respectful, no excuses or blame"],"rubricI18n":{"tr":["Görev: teşekkür, iki nokta, duygu, tarihli iki sonraki adım","Düzen: eylemden önce özet","Dil: dolaylı anlatım; sounds like + yan cümle; sözler için will","Üslup: saygılı; bahane ya da suçlama yok"],"fa":["کامل بودن کار: تشکر، دو نکته، احساس او، دو قدم بعدی با تاریخ","نظم: اول خلاصه، بعد اقدام","زبان: نقل قول غیرمستقیم؛ sounds like با جمله؛ will برای قول‌ها","لحن: محترمانه؛ بدون بهانه یا سرزنش"]},"portfolio":null,"parts":[{"t":{"en":"Thanks","tr":"Teşekkür","fa":"تشکر"},"find":["thank you"],"sample":"thanks for talking so openly"},{"t":{"en":"His two points","tr":"İki noktası","fa":"دو حرفش"},"find":["you said","you also said"],"sample":"extra shifts since March without being asked; a second forklift asked for two years ago"},{"t":{"en":"His feeling","tr":"Hissettiği","fa":"احساسش"},"find":["it sounds like","feels"],"sample":"the team feels overlooked"},{"t":{"en":"Two next steps with dates","tr":"Tarihleriyle iki sonraki adım","fa":"دو قدم بعدی با تاریخ"},"find":["as we agreed","by friday","on tuesday","will"],"sample":"overtime figures by Friday; meet the director on Tuesday"}]},"perspective":{"id":"c-hr-4-3-p","title":{"en":"Arash walking home","tr":"Eve yürüyen Arash","fa":"آرش در راه خانه"},"course":"hr","unit":"hr-4-3","type":"perspective","minSentences":3,"prompt":{"en":"Role reversal. You are Arash, walking home after the meeting. Write 3 sentences in first person: how do your twenty-two years at Atlas feel today, and what do you need HR to understand?","tr":"Rol değişimi. Toplantıdan sonra eve yürüyen Arash'sın. Birinci tekil şahısla 3 cümle yaz: Atlas'taki yirmi iki yılın bugün sana nasıl hissettiriyor ve İK'nın neyi anlamasına ihtiyacın var?","fa":"جایت را عوض کن. تو آرش هستی و بعد از جلسه پیاده به خانه برمی‌گردی. از زبان خودت سه جمله بنویس: امروز به آن بیست‌ودو سال کار در Atlas که فکر می‌کنی چه حسی داری، و دلت می‌خواهد واحد منابع انسانی چه چیزی را بفهمد؟"}},"exit":{"id":"c-hr-4-3-x","course":"hr","unit":"hr-4-3","type":"exit","items":[{"from":"hr-4-3","kind":"blank","prompt":"It sounds ___ the new rota is hard for your family.","options":["like","that","so"],"correct":0,"point":2,"why":{"en":"like: 'It sounds like' + a clause names what you heard. 'Sounds that' and 'sounds so' are not English.","tr":"like: 'It sounds like' + yan cümle duyduğunu adlandırır. 'Sounds that' ve 'sounds so' İngilizce değildir.","fa":"like درست است، چون It sounds like و بعد جمله چیزی را که شنیدی نام می‌برد. sounds that و sounds so انگلیسی نیستند."},"hint2":{"en":"After sounds, a whole clause follows (the new rota is hard for your family). One small word joins sounds to a clause.","tr":"sounds’tan sonra tam bir yan cümle geliyor (the new rota is hard for your family). sounds’u yan cümleye küçük bir kelime bağlar.","fa":"بعد از ⁨sounds⁩ یک جمله‌ی کامل آمده (⁨the new rota is hard for your family⁩). یک کلمه‌ی کوچک ⁨sounds⁩ را به جمله وصل می‌کند."}},{"from":"hr-4-3","kind":"blank","prompt":"That must be really ___.","options":["worrying","worried","worry"],"correct":0,"point":2,"why":{"en":"worrying: -ing describes the situation that causes the feeling. 'Worried' is how a person feels, and 'worry' is a verb or noun.","tr":"worrying: -ing duyguya yol açan durumu anlatır. 'Worried' kişinin ne hissettiğidir; 'worry' fiil ya da isimdir.","fa":"⁨worrying⁩ درست است، چون ⁨-ing⁩ موقعیتی را توصیف می‌کند که آن حس را می‌سازد. ⁨worried⁩ حس آدم است و ⁨worry⁩ فعل یا اسم."}},{"from":"hr-4-3","kind":"mcq","prompt":"What should you do BEFORE replying to a complaint?","options":["Explain the budget","Summarise the feelings and reasons you heard","Promise a solution"],"correct":1,"point":1,"why":{"en":"Summarise the feelings and reasons you heard: the person knows you listened. The budget or a quick promise comes too early.","tr":"Duyduğun duyguları ve nedenleri özetle: kişi dinlendiğini anlar. Bütçe ya da hızlı bir söz çok erken gelir.","fa":"حس‌ها و دلیل‌هایی را که شنیدی خلاصه کن تا طرف بفهمد گوش داده‌ای. حرف از بودجه یا قول سریع خیلی زود است."}},{"from":"hr-4-2","kind":"blank","prompt":"Please send the report ___ Friday.","options":["until","by","since"],"correct":1,"point":2,"why":{"en":"by: 'by Friday' is a deadline: no later than Friday. 'Until' is the whole time up to it, and 'since' looks back.","tr":"by: 'by Friday' bir son tarihtir: en geç cuma. 'Until' oraya kadar bütün süredir; 'since' geriye bakar.","fa":"by درست است، چون by Friday مهلت است: حداکثر تا جمعه. until تمام مدت تا آن موقع است و since به عقب نگاه می‌کند."},"hint2":{"en":"Sending happens once, at the latest on that day. Which word gives a deadline?","tr":"Bu, bir kez ve en geç o gün olacak bir şey. Hangi kelime son tarih bildirir?","fa":"فرستادن یک بار و حداکثر تا آن روز اتفاق می‌افتد. کدام کلمه مهلت را نشان می‌دهد؟"}},{"from":"hr-3-4","kind":"blank","prompt":"I'm afraid that on this ___, we will not be moving forward.","options":["occasion","time","moment"],"correct":0,"point":3,"why":{"en":"occasion: 'on this occasion' is the fixed polite phrase in rejections. 'On this time' and 'on this moment' are not English.","tr":"occasion: 'on this occasion' red yazılarında kullanılan sabit kibar ifadedir. 'On this time' ve 'on this moment' İngilizce değildir.","fa":"occasion درست است، چون on this occasion عبارت ثابت و مؤدبانه در جواب رد است. on this time و on this moment انگلیسی نیستند."},"hint2":{"en":"This is a fixed polite phrase in rejection emails: \"on this ...\". Which word completes it?","tr":"Bu, ret e-postalarında kullanılan kalıp bir kibar ifade: \"on this ...\". Hangi kelime onu tamamlar?","fa":"این یک عبارت مؤدبانه‌ی ثابت در ایمیل‌های رد است: «⁨on this ...⁩». کدام کلمه کاملش می‌کند؟"}},{"from":"hr-2-4","kind":"blank","prompt":"Hana speaks Turkish and English, ___ Karim speaks Arabic.","options":["therefore","whereas","despite"],"correct":1,"point":2,"why":{"en":"whereas: it contrasts two facts side by side. 'Therefore' gives a result, and 'despite' needs a noun.","tr":"whereas: iki bilgiyi yan yana karşılaştırır. 'Therefore' sonuç bildirir; 'despite' isim ister.","fa":"whereas درست است، چون دو واقعیت را در تقابل کنار هم می‌گذارد. therefore نتیجه را می‌گوید و despite اسم می‌خواهد."}}]}}; })(globalThis.COURSE_FILES = globalThis.COURSE_FILES || {});
